
========================================================================
  Test 1 -- concrete prefix walk (valid_next sharpness)
========================================================================
  empty (start)                    |valid| = 18  -> lit, partition, merge, identity, p, tau, sigma, gcd, ... (+10 more)
  GCD . (expecting Int)            |valid| = 18  -> lit, partition, merge, identity, p, tau, sigma, gcd, ... (+10 more)
  GCD LIT . (expecting Int)        |valid| = 18  -> lit, partition, merge, identity, p, tau, sigma, gcd, ... (+10 more)
  LET . (name slot demands LiteralInt) |valid| =  1  -> lit
  LET LIT LIT . (body slot, any Int) |valid| = 18  -> lit, partition, merge, identity, p, tau, sigma, gcd, ... (+10 more)
  SEQ . (variadic; END is valid here) |valid| = 19  -> end, lit, partition, merge, identity, p, tau, sigma, ... (+11 more)
  SEQ LIT . (still variadic)       |valid| = 19  -> end, lit, partition, merge, identity, p, tau, sigma, ... (+11 more)

  findings:
    * fresh/top-level slot admits 18 tokens (all Int producers)
    * LET's name slot admits ONLY LIT_INT (sharp constraint)
    * variadic slots include END as a terminator option

