========================================================================
  Test 3 -- unconstrained_random: 1000 samples, expect << 100%
========================================================================
  validated: 0/1000  (0.00%)
  (generation time: 27ms for 1000 programs)

  interpretation:
    * unconstrained generation is picking tokens without regard
      for the state machine -- arity / type / END-placement all
      violate frequently.  This is roughly what an unguided LLM
      token sampler produces if it's never seen LOVA training data.

========================================================================
  Test 4 -- the AI-friendly property, quantified
========================================================================
  constrained validate rate:    100.00%
  unconstrained validate rate:    0.00%
  delta (absolute):             +100.00 pp
  ratio (constrained / uncon.): infx

  claim (Axiom 3):
    A type-directed generator is, by construction, 100% valid.
    An unguided generator over the same token set is << 100%.
    The gap is load-bearing: this is the property that makes
    LOVA AI-friendly -- LLM samplers constrained to valid_next
    cannot emit ill-formed programs at all.

========================================================================
  Experiment 02 -- RESULT
========================================================================
  WIN.  Axiom 3 is operational: type-directed generation
  produces 100% well-typed programs; unguided generation
  produces only 0.0%.  Gap is load-bearing.
